# Python Study Platform — Full UX/UI Redesign

## 1. Overview & Context

The **"Python Learning HUB"** Stitch project (ID: `14570473170347892827`) serves as the **English-language UX/UI blueprint** for redesigning our Hebrew-language Python study platform. The Stitch design system — codenamed **"The Digital Atheneum"** — establishes a premium, dark-mode, editorial learning environment.

**Key principle:** We adopt the *visual language* from Stitch (colors, typography, spacing, elevation, component patterns) while **keeping all Hebrew content, lesson data, quiz logic, and exam functionality completely intact**.

---

## 2. Stitch Design System: "The Digital Atheneum"

The design system defines these foundational tokens:

### Color Palette (Dark Mode)
| Token | Hex | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| `background` | `#0b160f` | Page background (deep obsidian green) |
| `surface` | `#0b160f` | Base surface |
| `surface-container-low` | `#131e17` | Large secondary areas |
| `surface-container` | `#17221b` | Standard containers |
| `surface-container-high` | `#212d25` | Interactive cards |
| `surface-container-highest` | `#2c372f` | Active states |
| `surface-container-lowest` | `#06100a` | Code blocks, recessed areas |
| `primary` | `#d2ffd5` | Text on primary elements |
| `primary-container` | `#00f77b` | **Main accent** (neon green) |
| `on-surface` | `#d9e6da` | Primary text |
| `on-surface-variant` | `#b9cbb8` | Secondary text |
| `outline` | `#849584` | Subtle outlines |
| `outline-variant` | `#3b4b3c` | Ghost borders (15% opacity) |
| `error` | `#ffb4ab` | Error states |

### Typography
| Role | Font | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Display / Headlines** | Space Grotesk | Tight tracking (-0.02em), architectural precision |
| **Body** | Inter / Assistant Hebrew | 1.6x line-height for readability |
| **Labels** | Inter | All-caps, +0.05em letter-spacing |
| **Code** | Fira Code / Monospace | body-sm size |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> We must keep **Noto Sans Hebrew** as the primary body font for Hebrew text. Space Grotesk will be used for display/headline elements and English text. Inter remains for labels and UI chrome.

### Design Rules
- **No-Line Rule:** 1px borders are **prohibited** for sectioning. Use tonal background shifts instead.
- **Ghost Border:** If a border is needed for accessibility, use `outline-variant` at **15% opacity**.
- **Tonal Layering:** Elevation achieved through background color stacking, not shadows.
- **Glassmorphism:** Nav/floating elements use semi-transparent surfaces + `backdrop-blur(12-20px)`.
- **Signature Gradient:** CTAs use a 135° gradient from `primary-container` (#00f77b) → `primary-fixed` (#63ff93).
- **Asymmetric Margins:** Use uneven spacing for editorial layouts.
- **Generous Spacing:** Double the padding when in doubt.

